# playpick cell: mode=raid boss=marrow spec=paladin:holy style=wander
# size=25 difficulty=heroic view=390x844,touch save=fresh
#
# A fresh save only opens Bonegrinder 10-normal (progress.ts's chain), so
# reaching 25-heroic needs the invite-hash unlock (src/main.ts's invite
# handler unlocks whatever tier a link names). Since the hash names marrow
# itself -- the boss this cell actually wants -- `open #b=marrow&s=25&h=1`
# sets visiting=true and the class screen's button calls startFight()
# directly: a standalone mode=raid pull, exactly what this cell asks for
# (no need for the back->raid recipe, which is only for reaching an evening's
# own setup screen).
#
# Never run before on this combination: paladin:holy has only ever met gorged
# (Bloodgorged, wander, 25-heroic, 2026-09-25) and marrow under a mode=daily
# mislabel (the actual daily that day was crowns). This is the first time a
# genuinely-named mode=raid Bonegrinder pull has run under wander, and the
# first time a non-melee, non-tank spec has met Bonegrinder's bonestorm aura
# (#267's own open bug, "an aura on the boss that hurts everything near it
# while the boss wanders") under a style that neither stands still (idle,
# which this line's other Bonegrinder pulls have already shown wins clean)
# nor deliberately keeps distance (dodge/good/flee) -- wander picks a new
# random heading every twelve steps and presses a random ability slot
# regardless of where the boss or its aura are.
open #b=marrow&s=25&h=1
targets
shot roster
tap class:paladin:holy
targets
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start

play wander 80
bill
state
shot mid1

play wander 80
bill
state
shot mid2

play wander 80
bill
state
shot end
says
